@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+---
+id: task-002-record-createdat-and-updatedat-for-each-task
+type: task
+title: "Record createdAt and updatedAt for each task"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Show how old a task is, and what changed recently: every task needs a `createdAt` and an `updatedAt`, as
+ISO-8601 date-time strings. The two are equal when a task is added; completing, reopening, renaming,
+tagging or untagging a task sets its `updatedAt` to the time of the change.
+
+## What changed
+
+- `Task` (`src/domain/task.ts`) gained `createdAt: string` and `updatedAt: string`. `createTask` now takes
+  a third parameter, `now`, and stamps both fields with it, to stay clock-free per
+  `r3-no-clock-or-randomness`.
+- `completeTask`, `reopenTask`, `renameTask`, `addTag` and `removeTag` (`src/domain/task.ts`) each gained
+  a `now` parameter and set `updatedAt` to it; `createdAt` is untouched by all of them.
+- `TaskList` (`src/domain/list.ts`): `add`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag` and `untag` each gained
+  a required `now` parameter, threaded through to the matching domain function.
+- Tests added to `test/list.test.ts`: `createdAt` equals `updatedAt` on add; `updatedAt` advances while
+  `createdAt` stays fixed across a complete, reopen, rename, tag and untag; a refused change (completing
+  an already-done task, renaming onto a duplicate title) leaves `updatedAt` unchanged. Every existing call
+  to a mutating `TaskList` method was updated to pass a `now`. Written and confirmed failing before the
+  implementation (red, then green).
+
+See decision-log `dl-002-timestamps-passed-in-by-the-caller-not-read-from-the-clock-in-the-domain` for
+the design rationale.
+
+## Verification
+
+`npm test`: 13/13 passing.
+</content>
